# Docker Fixes Implementation Plan

The goal is to fix Docker build errors reported by the user: a casing warning in the backend Dockerfile and a TypeScript error in the frontend build.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile.backend](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/Dockerfile.backend)
- Change `as builder` to `AS builder` on line 4 for consistency and to silence the warning.

### Frontend
#### [MODIFY] [projectListPage.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/frontend/src/pages/projectListPage.tsx)
- Remove the unused `useEffect` import to fix the `TS6133` error preventing the build.

### Backend (Startup Fix)
#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile.backend](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/Dockerfile.backend)
- Change venv creation to `/opt/venv` in builder stage to fix absolute path issues causing `alembic: not found`.
- Fix `ImportError` by converting relative imports (e.g., `from ..database`, `from .routers`) to absolute imports (e.g., `from database`, `from routers`) throughout the backend code, as the Docker container runs the code from the root `/app` directory.
- Update [.env](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/.env) to set a valid `SMTP_PORT` (587) to prevent Pydantic validation errors on empty strings.

### Nginx (Runtime Fix)
#### [MODIFY] [nginx.conf](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/nginx.conf)
- Remove duplicate global directives (`include mime.types`, `default_type`) from [nginx.conf](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/nginx.conf) because it is included inside the `http` block of the main Nginx configuration, causing collision errors.

### Nginx (Startup Permission Fix)
#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile.frontend](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/Dockerfile.frontend)
- Add command to touch and chown `/var/run/nginx.pid` so the non-root `nginx` user can write to it.

